{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"**Patchset 2 pushed** to Gerrit change 2658 (`939dab422518`), rebased onto current `origin/main` (`084e753d30df`; 2657/2656/2653 had landed). Change-Id preserved — same change, new patchset. Both prior votes were auto-outdated by the push, as expected.\n\nAddresses the `maintainability` advisory on `scripts/check_terraform_tree_currency.py`: a tree whose merge base with the tip IS the tip strictly CONTAINS it, so it is now reported as **\"ahead of\"** the tracked branch, not \"diverged from\" it. The reviewer's framing is right and I took it as more than cosmetic — calling an ahead tree diverged is the same collapse of distinct states, one level down, that this gate's three-valued exit code exists to refuse; an operator would go hunting for a divergence that is not there.\n\nTwo things moved with the label, because a wrong label with a right remedy is only half-fixed:\n\n- **The remedy line.** \"Fast-forward this tree (`git merge --ff-only`)\" cannot work on a tree that already contains the tip. Ahead and diverged trees now get \"plan from a worktree at `<label>`\" instead.\n- **The explanatory sentence.** The behind-case text (\"resources declared on the branch but absent here read as *No changes*\") is simply false for an ahead tree; that case now says it plans commits the tracked branch does not carry, so a clean result is evidence about UNLANDED work, not about the branch.\n\nExit-code semantics are unchanged: an ahead tree is still `EXIT_STALE` in `tip` mode and still `EXIT_CURRENT` in `ancestor` mode.\n\nPinned by two new tests in `tests/unit/test_terraform_tree_currency.py` — `test_an_ahead_tree_is_called_ahead_not_diverged` (asserts \"ahead of\", asserts \"diverged\"/\"behind\" absent, and asserts the fast-forward advice is gone) and `test_a_diverged_tree_is_still_called_diverged` as its control, so narrowing \"diverged\" cannot quietly empty it. Both were RED against patchset 1, verified by running them in a throwaway worktree at the old commit."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788586987738527792,"uuid":"8359ca9e-04a8-4c9f-96d9-402a53e4a229"}